([PROBLEM 3: Defense-in-Depth Cybersecurity Architecture Design]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Context: Design an enterprise multi-tier cybersecurity architecture to defend an) Tj
T*
(electronic health records \(EHR\) database against modern Ransomware attacks.) Tj
T*
(Tiered Defense Implementation Protocol:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Perimeter Tier \(Network Ingress\): Next-Generation Firewall \(NGFW\) with deep) Tj
T*
(packet inspection; Web Application Firewall \(WAF\) blocking SQL injection and) Tj
T*
(cross-site scripting \(XSS\); DDoS mitigation shield.) Tj
T*
(* 2. Network Demilitarized Zone \(DMZ\): Isolate public-facing web servers from backend) Tj
T*
(databases. Zero-trust network microsegmentation preventing lateral lateral movement) Tj
T*
(between subnets.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Endpoint Tier: Endpoint Detection and Response \(EDR\) software with behavioral) Tj
T*
(heuristic monitoring to detect unauthorized bulk cryptographic file modifications;) Tj
T*
(mandatory application whitelisting.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Identity & Access Management \(IAM\): Role-Based Access Control \(RBAC\);) Tj
T*
(Multi-Factor Authentication \(MFA\) via FIDO2 hardware keys; strictly adhere to the) Tj
T*
(Principle of Least Privilege \(PoLP\).) Tj
T*
(* 5. Data & Storage Tier: End-to-end AES-256 encryption for data at rest and TLS 1.3) Tj
T*
(for data in transit; immutable, air-gapped write-once-read-many \(WORM\) offline) Tj
T*
(backups to guarantee recovery without paying ransom.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
([PROBLEM 4: Edge Computing vs Cloud Latency Analysis in Autonomous Systems]) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
/F2 9.5 Tf
(-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
(Problem Statement: An autonomous vehicle traveling at 100 km/h \(27.78 m/s\) utilizes) Tj
T*
(high-resolution LiDAR and cameras to detect unexpected road obstacles. Compare obstacle) Tj
T*
(reaction distance between: \(1\) Local On-Board Edge Processing \(latency 15 ms\), and \(2\)) Tj
T*
(Cloud Datacenter Processing \(uplink + compute + downlink latency 180 ms\).) Tj
T*
(Mathematical Derivation:) Tj
T*
(* 1. Reaction Distance Formula: Distance = Velocity \(m/s\) x Total Decision Latency) Tj
T*
(\(s\).) Tj
T*
(* 2. Local Edge Computing Processing:) Tj
T*
(- Total latency = 15 ms = 0.015 seconds.) Tj
T*
(- Reaction distance = 27.78 m/s x 0.015 s = 0.417 meters \(approx 42 cm\). Vehicle) Tj
T*
(initiates emergency braking within less than half a meter of obstacle detection.) Tj
T*
(* 3. Centralized Cloud Datacenter Processing:) Tj
T*
(- Total latency = 180 ms = 0.180 seconds.) Tj
T*
(- Reaction distance = 27.78 m/s x 0.180 s = 5.00 meters.) Tj
T*
(* 4. Engineering Impact: Centralized cloud processing introduces an unacceptable) Tj
T*
(5-meter blind delay before brakes can be applied, proving why life-critical) Tj
T*
(autonomous systems mandate localized edge computing.) Tj
T*
